-- title:
--   Divisibility from Fr^m acting trivially on Frᵈ-fixed elements
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero and $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ an irreducible element such that the quotient $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and the principal ideals $(r)$ and $(\pi)$ of $\mathcal{O}$ coincide. Let $\mathrm{Onr}$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, and let $\mathrm{Fr}$ be an automorphism of $\mathrm{Onr}$ as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra. Write $\mathfrak{m}$ for the ideal of $\mathrm{Onr}$ generated by the image of $\pi$. Assume: $\mathrm{Onr}$ is $\mathfrak{m}$-adically complete; $\mathfrak{m}$ is maximal; every $x \in \mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies $p(x) \in \mathfrak{m}$ for some monic $p \in \mathcal{O}[X]$; every monic $p \in \mathrm{Onr}[X]$ of positive degree has some $x \in \mathrm{Onr}$ with $p(x) \in \mathfrak{m}$; and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) - x^{r} \in \mathfrak{m}$ for all $x$. Let $k$ be a field which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, let $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to k$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, and let $d, m$ be integers. If $\psi(\mathrm{Fr}^{m} y) = \psi(y)$ for every $y \in \mathrm{Onr}$ with $\mathrm{Fr}^{d} y = y$, then $d$ divides $m$.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement that pins down the exponent in the Frobenius twist used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld realignment: in the axiomatic model of a complete unramified local ring with residue field of prime order $r$ and its residual Frobenius lift, the $\mathrm{Fr}^{d}$-fixed part is large enough that $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$ can act trivially on it, as measured by any $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map to a field, only when $d \mid m$ (in particular $m = 0$ when $d = 0$). It is invoked by [`CerednikDrinfeld.cerednikDrinfeld_realign_of_frobTwist_eq_on_fixed`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.cerednikDrinfeld_realign_of_frobTwist_eq_on_fixed).
